<aiml version="1.0">

<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS WWIV BBS SOFTWARE</pattern>
<template>WWIV is a bulletin board system software package created by Wayne Bell in 1984. It was originally written in BASIC and later rewritten in C.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS WWIVNET</pattern>
<template>WWIVnet is WWIV's built-in message network, letting WWIV boards exchange mail and messages with each other.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT PLATFORMS DOES WWIV RUN ON</pattern>
<template>WWIV originally ran on MS-DOS. Modern WWIV 5 runs on Windows and Linux.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>IS WWIV STILL DEVELOPED</pattern>
<template>Yes. WWIV is open source and still developed as WWIV 5, maintained on GitHub.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT MADE WWIV DIFFERENT FROM OTHER BBS SOFTWARE</pattern>
<template>WWIV shipped its source code, so sysops could customize and modify their boards — a major selling point.</template>
</category>
</aiml>
